{%- comment -%}
  Whether a tool is offered to a model (MCP Apps visibility, docs/mcp-apps.md). A tool is
  model-visible unless its manifest declares ui.visibility without "model": such an
  app-only tool exists for an MCP Apps card. Over MCP it is listed and callable only for
  a client that declared MCP Apps (helpers/protocol/apps_client), whose host keeps it
  from the model; the server cannot tell a card's call from a model's. It is left out of
  the in-app agent's tool list and refused by the in-process invoke.

  @param {object} manifest - a validated manifest from queries/registry/load
  @return {boolean}
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign visibility = manifest.ui.visibility
  if visibility == blank
    return true
  endif
  if visibility contains 'model'
    return true
  endif
  return false
%}
